          "title": "You'll want to know: সমস্যা",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "সমস্যা — sômôsyā — \"a problem\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "তোমার কোনো সমস্যা হলে আমাকে বলো। tomār kono sômôsyā hôle āmāke bôlo. If you have any problem, tell me."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "সমস্যা (sômôsyā) is Sanskrit samasyā, a part of a verse given to someone else to complete, a kind of puzzle (Monier-Williams). Bengali widened the puzzle to any problem; that widening is not in the dictionary."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
