          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "উতরে যাওয়া — utre jāoyā — \"to come through; to get through (a test)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "অনেক ঝামেলার পরে আমরা উতরে গেলাম। ônek jhāmelār pôre āmrā utre gelām. After a lot of trouble, we came through."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (he/she …): সেই পরিকল্পনাটা উতরে গেল, sei pôrikôlpônāṭā utre gelô."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "উতরে যাওয়া (utre jāoyā) is the -এ form of উতরা 'to cross, to get over' (CDIAL 1770 lists Bengali utarā) with যাওয়া: to get across a difficulty to the other side. The sense 'to pass a test' is a Bengali use."
            }
          ]
        },
